57=12.	The scent and fragance in the house are like an aromatic cedar forest. 
61=13.	In the house, there is beer, there is good beer. There is sweet beer, and honeyed cakes, ……. 

{A.14 = 14-24}
65=14.	Let your acquaintances come! 
69=15.	Let your dear ones come! 
73=16.	Let your father and grandfather come! 
77=17.	Let the sons of your elder brother and the sons of your younger brother come! 
81=18.	Let your little ones come, and your big ones too! 
85=19.	Let your wife and your children come! 
89=20.	Let your friends and companions come! 
93=21.	Let your brother-in-law and your father-in-law come! 
97=22.	Let the crowd by the side of your front door come! 
101=23.	Don't leave your friends' children outside! 
105=24.	Don't leave your neighbours outside, whoever they may be! 

{A.25 = 25-33}
109=25.	Enter, my beloved son! Enter, my fine son! Don't let the day go by, 
113=26.	don't let the night come! The moonlight should not enter that house! 
117=27.	But if the day has gone by and the night comes, 
121=28.	enter and I will let you relax there; I have made the grounds suitable for you! 
125=29.	Inside, 
129=30.	I have fixed up a seat for you. 
133=31.	My fish, 
137=32.	no one who sleeps there will be disturbed; 
141=33.	no one who sits there will get involved in a quarrel. 

{A.34 = 34-39}
145=34.	Enter, my beloved son! 
149=35.	Enter, my fine son! 
153=36.	As if you were in a river with brackish water, don't go investigating any canals! 
157=37.	As if you were in silt settled on the riverbed, may you not be able to get up! 
161=38.	As if you were in flowing water, you should not fix your bed! 
165=39.	The moonlight should not enter that house! 

{A.40 = 40-44}
169=40.	And may you not succeed in getting away: face towards me! 
173=41.	And may you not succeed in getting away like a …… to your lair: face towards me! 
177=42.	And may you not succeed in getting away like a dog to where you go sniffing: face towards me! 
181=43.	And may you not succeed in getting away like a …… to where you ……: face towards me! 
185=44.	And may you not succeed in getting away like a bull to your cattle-pen, like a sheep to your sheepfold: face towards me! 

